		int "id" [=[ {} ]=],
	}
	ns "HUD"
	returns "void"
	doc [[!
<summary>
This function shows various HUD (Heads-up Display) components.

Listed below are the integers and the corresponding HUD component.

*   1 : WANTED_STARS
*   2 : WEAPON_ICON
*   3 : CASH
*   4 : MP_CASH
*   5 : MP_MESSAGE
*   6 : VEHICLE_NAME
*   7 : AREA_NAME
*   8 : VEHICLE_CLASS
*   9 : STREET_NAME
*   10 : HELP_TEXT
*   11 : FLOATING_HELP_TEXT\_1
*   12 : FLOATING_HELP_TEXT\_2
*   13 : CASH_CHANGE
*   14 : RETICLE
*   15 : SUBTITLE_TEXT
*   16 : RADIO_STATIONS
*   17 : SAVING_GAME
*   18 : GAME_STREAM
*   19 : WEAPON_WHEEL
*   20 : WEAPON_WHEEL_STATS
*   21 : HUD_COMPONENTS
*   22 : HUD_WEAPONS

These integers also work for the [`HIDE_HUD_COMPONENT_THIS_FRAME`](#\_0x6806C51AD12B83B8) native, but instead hides the HUD component.
</summary>
	]]

